    quotes: ['A part of all you earn is yours to keep.'],
    criticism: 'The archaic parable style irritates many readers and pads a short message. Advice to own property is stated as a law when it is a conditional decision, particularly at UK prices. And it is silent on everything modern — index funds, pensions, ISAs, inflation — so it must be paired with something current to be actionable.',
    verdict: 'Read it in an evening, or read a summary. Best suited to someone who has never saved consistently; unnecessary if you already run a budget and invest automatically.',
